The agent type this mesh was baked for. The .navmesh file does not
carry the scene's agent list, so a loader that knows it names the mesh;
otherwise it reads from the bake settings.

Async bake. Hand off a `Snapshot` produced on the main thread —
the returned future runs the Recast pipeline on a worker thread
and yields an AsyncResult with a fresh NavMeshAsset on success.

The optional progress block is updated by the worker thread; the
caller polls it each frame to drive a progress bar. It must
outlive the future (a shared_ptr handles that without thinking).

Usage:
auto snap = SnapshotScene(scene);
auto progress = std::make_shared<BakeProgress>();
auto fut  = BakeAsync(std::move(snap), settings, progress);
// ... later, on main thread:
if (fut.wait_for(0s) == ready) {
auto r = fut.get();
if (r.info.success) scene.SetNavMesh(r.asset);
